  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Total obligations are $14.3B for Alabama in FY2026 to date. Award count is 89,430 and average award size is $160K. Obligations fell 21.2% year over year. The Department of Defense obligated $9.4B, making Defense the dominant buying agency by a wide margin. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $2.6B, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs at $503M and the Department of State at $500M. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION and THE BOEING COMPANY each received $1.2B, and DYNETICS, INC. received $1B. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is the largest industry at $3.8B, and Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is second at $2.6B. Fiscal-year history shows obligations moved from $13.1B in FY21 to $18.1B in FY25 and then to $14.3B in FY26. Current-year totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date reporting.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated is federal spending in Alabama by agency?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $9.4B, so Defense accounts for the largest share of Alabama obligations. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $2.6B, and combined smaller agencies like the Department of Veterans Affairs and the Department of State each obligated about $500M. Other agencies with meaningful activity include the General Services Administration at $465M and the Department of Homeland Security at $439M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and industries dominate Alabama contracting?",
        "body": "LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION and THE BOEING COMPANY each received $1.2B and DYNETICS, INC. received $1B, placing them at the top of vendor ranks. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is the largest industry at $3.8B, followed by Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing at $2.6B and Engineering Services at $1.2B. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is notable at $1B."
      }
    ]
  },
